# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback (Phase 8 — deployment readiness).
#
# Without this, opening a client-side route directly (e.g. a customer
# bookmarks /orders/42, or refreshes /admin/products) returns a real 404
# from Cloudflare Pages' static file server, because no actual
# orders/42/index.html file exists — React Router only ever runs AFTER
# index.html has loaded. This rule tells Pages to serve index.html for any
# path that doesn't match a real static file, so React Router's <Routes>
# can then take over client-side and render the correct page (including
# /menu/:id, /orders/:id, /admin/*, etc — every dynamic route in App.jsx).
#
# 200 (not 301/302) is required — a redirect status would change the URL
# instead of just serving different content at the same URL.
/*    /index.html   200
